llboard" 200.","title":"MTV Unplugged 2.0"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" It is the only Dashboard Confessional LP album with a platinum certification.","title":"MTV Unplugged 2.0"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Rooftops and Invitations" is a download-only single from the album "Dusk and Summer" by Dashboard Confessional.","title":"Rooftops and Invitations"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The song was written by the lead singer of Dashboard Confessional, Chris Carrabba.","title":"Rooftops and Invitations"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" "Rooftops and Invitations" was released to radio on August 29, 2006.","title":"Rooftops and Invitations"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Don't Wait" is the first single from the album "Dusk and Summer" by Dashboard Confessional.","title":"Don't Wait (Dashboard Confessional song)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The song was written by the lead singer of Dashboard Confessional, Chris Carrabba.","title":"Don't Wait (Dashboard Confessional song)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is about living for the day, that 'the moment is now'.","title":"Don't Wait (Dashboard Confessional song)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" "Don't Wait" was released to radio on May 23, 2006.","title":"Don't Wait (Dashboard Confessional song)"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Escanaba Firing Line is a Michigan rock band formed in 2002 that has released live albums such as Live at Short's (2006) and Live at The Belmont (2010), while Dashboard Confessional is a different band whose live album MTV Unplugged 2.0 (2002) went platinum and who issued singles like “Rooftops and Invitations” and “Don’t Wait” in 2006.
